Description: Auto DJ: order the queue by key and tempo ("Harmonic")
 A "Harmonic" button next to "Shuffle" in the Auto DJ view, and the control
 [AutoDJ],sort_harmonic, order the Auto DJ queue (or the selected rows) for
 mixing: compatible keys on the Camelot / Open Key wheel (same key, +-1 step,
 relative major/minor) and small tempo changes (half/double tempo counts as
 the same; beyond +-8 % costs extra; going down costs more than going up).
 Greedy, from the track playing (or the next track of a running Auto DJ,
 which stays first) or else from the slowest track. Tracks keep their key:
 nothing is pitch shifted. Uses the key and BPM from Mixxx's analysis.
 The ordering is in library/autodj/harmonicorder.h (header only, unit tested);
 PlaylistDAO::reorderTracks() writes the new positions in one transaction.
Author: DecksmithOS
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-21
